@startuml
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
title Sweep — async issue-to-PR worker (OUTDATED shape)
' Product: Sweep
' URL: https://sweep.dev/
' Level: 4
' Status: The issue-to-PR architecture drawn here is the 2023-24 product. As of 2026-09 sweep.dev
'         sells a JetBrains IDE plugin (autocomplete + inline agent) and the GitHub-bot positioning
'         is gone from the homepage. Kept as a dated snapshot of the webhook-driven async-worker
'         pattern, which is the reason this study-case exists; do not cite it as Sweep's current shape.

package "Sweep (Async Worker)" {
    [GitHub Webhook Handler] as HOOK
    [Search Engine\n(Vector + Lexical)] as SEARCH
    [Planner] as PLAN
    [Pull Request Generator] as PR
    [CI/CD\n(GitHub Actions)] as EVAL
}

HOOK --> SEARCH : "Issue -> Code Search"
SEARCH --> PLAN : "Relevant Files"
PLAN --> PR : "Generate Code & PR"
PR --> EVAL : "Run Tests"
EVAL --> PLAN : "Fix Failures"

note right of HOOK
  Stateless between events.
  Driven by Issue comments.
end note
@enduml
